    <item>
      <title>Version 1.0.13</title>
      <description>&lt;div style="font:13px -apple-system,system-ui,sans-serif;line-height:1.45"&gt;&lt;h3 style="font-size:13px;margin:10px 0 4px"&gt;Improved&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul style="margin:0;padding-left:18px"&gt;&lt;li&gt;Sharing comes back on its own after your Mac wakes from sleep.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The pair address updates by itself when you switch Wi-Fi or turn on Internet Sharing.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;When nobody is watching for a minute, the extra screen steps aside so your cursor stays on your Mac. It comes back as soon as the car connects.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;One screen at a time: if a second device opens the pair address, it's told the Mac is already in use.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Pairing code settings are now a single switch, and the code is shown in the sidebar.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;h3 style="font-size:13px;margin:10px 0 4px"&gt;Fixed&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;ul style="margin:0;padding-left:18px"&gt;&lt;li&gt;Touch could stop responding after the connection dropped and came back.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;The pairing code is now required on every connection when it's turned on.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Skip back and skip forward were swapped in the video player.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top:10px"&gt;&lt;a href="https://tesktop.com/changelog/#v1-0-13"&gt;All changes&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
      <pubDate>Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:45:06 +0000</pubDate>
